The `useEffect` hook is used to perform side effects in functional components. In this case, it's used to update the document's title whenever the `count` state changes.

The `useEffect` hook takes two arguments:

1. A function that contains the code to run the side effect. In this case, it's updating the document's title.

2. An array of dependencies. The side effect will run whenever any value in this array changes. In this case, the dependency array contains `count`, so the side effect will run whenever `count` changes.

So, when the `count` state changes (for example, when the button is clicked and the `setCount` function is called), the `useEffect` hook "reacts" to this change and runs the side effect, updating the document's title to include the new count.

